<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mons Lactarius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">552 or 553</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554">Gothic War (535–554)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> Lactarius was fought near Mount Vesuvius in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a> in 552 or 553 between the Byzantine army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narses">Narses</a> and the last Ostrogothic king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teia">Teia</a>. After a stand-off of about two months the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> attacked, and Teia was killed in the fighting. The defeat marked the end of the Ostrogothic Kingdom as an organised power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-lactarius.jpg" alt="Battle of Mons Lactarius" width="320" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A.Cython · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gothic_War_army_movements_second_phase.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
